---
title: Code review of one subtask
---
flowchart TD
    classDef human fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#8a6d3b,color:#000
    classDef role fill:#d9edf7,stroke:#31708f,color:#000
    classDef channel fill:#dff0d8,stroke:#3c763d,color:#000
    classDef stop fill:#eeeeee,stroke:#777,color:#000

    classDef gate fill:#f2dede,stroke:#a94442,color:#000

    START(["Human asks for a review"]):::human
    CR["Code Reviewer — diff-level scope,<br/>one subtask's worth of change"]:::role
    FIND{"Any subtask at 👀 Review<br/>in .claude/task.md?"}
    NONE["Nothing to review. Say so and stop —<br/>do not review the tree anyway, and do not<br/>guess from what looks recently touched"]:::stop
    DIRTY{"Is the working tree dirty?<br/>git status --porcelain"}
    CLEAN["Nothing to review. The subtask claims to be<br/>finished but its change is not in the tree —<br/>committed before review, or never made.<br/>Name it and stop. Do not search git log"]:::stop
    LOCATE["The uncommitted tree IS that subtask's work —<br/>the human commits after each accepted<br/>subtask, so no attribution is needed.<br/>git diff, plus untracked files whole.<br/>Only the new code and documentation;<br/>never anything already committed"]

    C1["1. Is it FINISHED?<br/>every part of the subtask, not the easy parts.<br/>A dropped bullet, a todo! left where the work<br/>should be, an edge case the subtask named<br/>and the code ignores"]
    C2["2. Is it CORRECT?<br/>CLAUDE.md invariants first: log before page,<br/>latch ordering, one write guard per page<br/>per thread, all-zero pages valid, page-0<br/>header logged, errors logged once"]
    C3["3. Is it the RIGHT SOLUTION?<br/>wrong layer, machinery the tree already has,<br/>an abstraction that blocks the next milestone,<br/>a special case where the general one was<br/>cheaper. CI can never ask this"]
    C4["4. Is it WELL MADE?<br/>CLAUDE.md conventions, Rust practice,<br/>naming, error handling, logging levels,<br/>no user data above DEBUG,<br/>no comments in .rs"]
    C5["All four asked of the DOCUMENTATION too:<br/>does each .MD still describe its .rs?<br/>Usage Example still valid? Did the change<br/>falsify a crate README or CLAUDE.md?<br/>check_docs.sh has the mechanical half"]
    C6["NOT yours: tests, and whether the gate<br/>was run. Both are the Coder's and both<br/>are automated — CI reports them louder<br/>and sooner than you could"]:::stop

    FOUND{"Any finding?"}
    BACKTO["Move the marker back to 🚧 In Progress.<br/>The same subtask gets finished, rather than<br/>its defects becoming new work.<br/>The marker only — the explanation lives<br/>in the problems.md entries and the reply"]
    SETDONE["Move the marker to ✅ Done in .claude/task.md.<br/>Only this role sets it, and only here.<br/>The marker only — never a note beside it,<br/>never a word of the description"]:::gate
    BUGS[".claude/problems.md — append one entry:<br/>P-n from the 'Next entry:' line,<br/>Created by: Code Reviewer, Reason,<br/>Description, How to prevent in future.<br/>Prevention is a lint, a test or a CI step,<br/>never 'be careful next time'.<br/>It is read once and deleted when scheduled,<br/>so it must stand on its own"]:::channel
    BACK(["Coder finishes the same subtask;<br/>preventions the entries name are<br/>scheduled separately<br/>— see agent-flow-problem-lifecycle.mmd"]):::stop

    OK["Say so plainly. Write nothing to problems.md"]
    HUMAN["Human reviews and commits"]:::human
    MORE{"Subtasks left in the Order Plan?"}
    NEXTSUB(["Coder takes the next subtask"]):::stop
    MSREVIEW(["Milestone Reviewer<br/>— see agent-flow-milestone-review.mmd"]):::stop

    START --> CR --> FIND
    FIND -- no --> NONE
    FIND -- yes --> DIRTY
    DIRTY -- no --> CLEAN
    DIRTY -- yes --> LOCATE --> C1 --> C2 --> C3 --> C4 --> C5 --> FOUND
    C5 -.-> C6
    FOUND -- yes --> BUGS --> BACKTO --> BACK
    FOUND -- no --> SETDONE --> OK --> HUMAN --> MORE
    MORE -- yes --> NEXTSUB
    MORE -- no --> MSREVIEW